    {
      "title": "OpenAEV Implant: actions of the Threat Arsenal",
      "text": "The platform writes one contract per payload of the Threat Arsenal and per injector that runs payloads, the OpenAEV Implant among them, and rewrites it when the payload changes. Each argument of the payload adds a required field under its key (a targeted-asset argument adds the asset, the property to read and a separator), and a command payload adds the choice of an obfuscator. Its expectations are prevention, detection and vulnerability; those the payload names are predefined. The targets are endpoints of the platforms the payload runs on, through an executor. Offered in atomic testing.",
      "columns": [
        "Field",
        "Key",
        "Type",
        "Required",
        "Default and notes"
      ],
      "rows": [
